 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to authorizing the division of\nminority and women's business development to accept the DD Form 214 issued by\nthe United States department of defense upon retirement, separation, or\ndischarge from active duty in the armed forces of the United States as proof\nof the race or ethnicity and certain personal information of an applicant for\npurposes of certification of the applicant's business as a minority-owned\nbusiness",
    "basePrintNo": "S7891",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7891-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §314, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7891\n\nSPONSOR: LITTLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the executive law, in relation to\nauthorizing the division of minority and women's business development to\naccept the DD Form 214 issued by the United States department of defense\nupon retirement, separation, or discharge from active duty in the armed\nforces of the United States as proof of the race or ethnicity and\ncertain personal information of an applicant for purposes of certif-\nication of the applicant's business as a minority-owned business\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to create a process for minority veterans to\nbecome recognized as a certified minority and women-owned business\nenterprise (MWBE).\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends section 314 of the executive law by includ-\ning a procedure which allows past military service members to confirm\ntheir race or ethnicity, date of birth and verification of address in\nthe interest of being recognized as a certified minority business by the\nsubmission of the DD Form 214. The director shall promulgate rules and\nregulations to set forth criteria for the acceptance of the DD Form 214.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill intends to enable veterans to utilize their DD214 form for the\npurpose of providing municipal corporations and State agencies, a form\nof identification for enrollment in MWBE programs.  In certain cases,\nveteran minority-owned business enterprises have been denied access to\nenrollment as their classified race or ethnicity even with proof present\non DD Form 214, a federal document, which was not listed as valid source\nof verification.  Enactment of this bill would alleviate certain verifi-\ncation burden veterans may have when looking to qualify for MWBE\nprograms.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law; provided, however, that the amendments to section 314 of\nthe executive law made by section one of this act shall not affect the\nexpiration of such section and shall be deemed expired therewith.\n",
